{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Noah","id":"360967589511561218","is_bot":0,"username":"king.crusader"},"author_id":"360967589511561218","channel_id":"863631111585660938","content":"Quick question regarding the arbiter class\n\nDo the trick shots not work with the archery fighting style due to them not being considered ranged attacks? Or do they still benefit from those types of things","created_at":"2021-08-17T17:11:19.640000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"877238176773734401","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Noah","id":"360967589511561218","is_bot":0,"username":"king.crusader"},"author_id":"360967589511561218","channel_id":"863631111585660938","content":"Also a different question. Do people inside beads of force still take fall damage or would it be like a safe bubble for us?\n\nIt states that no attack or effect other than breathable air can pass through. But since falling and the ground isn't an attack I'd want to clarify","created_at":"2021-08-17T17:26:31.184000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"877242000066359338","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"863631111585660938","content":"this is correct... trick shots are more like non magical cantrips","created_at":"2021-08-17T17:31:57.102000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"877243367065534514","reply_to_id":"877238176773734401","thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Noah","id":"360967589511561218","is_bot":0,"username":"king.crusader"},"author_id":"360967589511561218","channel_id":"863631111585660938","content":"Got it thanks","created_at":"2021-08-17T17:32:41.995000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"877243555360436254","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"863631111585660938","content":"so this is assuming a creature takes the 5d4 force and is inside..... as for fall damage... thats a more interesting question.... gimme a few to look up rulings and such","created_at":"2021-08-17T17:34:38.827000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"877244045389357168","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"863631111585660938","content":"Since bead of force is like Resilient Sphere, Having read the arguments both for and against fall damage, I would say no fall damage.\n\nMy reasoning is as follows: The kinetic energy transfer from a fall would be an external force which can not affect the person(s) inside.  Likewise since the sphere weighs 1 lb, It shows that the internal environment doesn't equate to the external.  It could be argued that the person(s) inside are either always standing at the bottom of the sphere due to it having its own version of gravity, or that world's gravity (an external force) has no affect, and therefore they couldn't even push on the side of the sphere.  So I would say the argument for no fall damage is greater than the argument for fall damage.","created_at":"2021-08-17T17:42:24.634000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"877245999125520424","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Noah","id":"360967589511561218","is_bot":0,"username":"king.crusader"},"author_id":"360967589511561218","channel_id":"863631111585660938","content":"Cool thanks","created_at":"2021-08-17T17:59:13.133000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"877250229076893696","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
